== PART W: the manager's reading 'the withdrawn looped-warning is the existing label.unset under the one rule'.
   looped-warning's trigger: a bare condition after the pattern reads a label whose group is inside a loop;
   label.unset's: the label CAN BE UNSET where the condition reads it (here: some path reaching it, over the pool)
W `/(?:(?<h>\d);)*/ & (h: <5)`: looped-warning fires ; label.unset fires
W `/(?:(?<h>\d);)+/ & (h: <5)`: looped-warning fires ; label.unset silent   <- they differ
W `/(?:(?<h>\d)?;)+/ & (h: <5)`: looped-warning fires ; label.unset fires
W `/(?<h>\d)?;/ & (h: <5)`: looped-warning silent ; label.unset fires   <- they differ
W `/(?<h>\d);/ & (h: <5)`: looped-warning silent ; label.unset silent

